All 21 solvable primitive groups of degrees 2 to 9 have the required chain-abundant subset sizes.  The singleton exceptions are PrimitiveGroup(9,5), (C3 x C3):QD16 = AGammaL(1,9), and PrimitiveGroup(9,7), the affine group AGL(2,3).
Each of the 501 solvable transitive groups of degrees 2 to 15 has an abundant subset.
